Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.72,0:00:05.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew you would come.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.48,0:00:08.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure you know how I feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.75,0:00:12.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know some things have happened\N between you guys and me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.64,0:00:15.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but you and I are \Nessentially very similar.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.26,0:00:21.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if that's the reason why Edward-kun doesn't want to see me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.30,0:00:25.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother doesn't want to use the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.82,0:00:28.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.78,0:00:31.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You brothers were, you know...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.07,0:00:35.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We journeyed together to \Nget back that which we had lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.70,0:00:37.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's everything that we are.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.55,0:00:54.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you in pain, Nina?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.26,0:00:56.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.75,0:00:59.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All preparations \Nare in order now...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.11,0:01:10.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your body, as well as the lives which were provided by many animals...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.93,0:01:13.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All that's left now is to join them all together
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.25,0:01:16.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,with the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.44,0:01:21.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How did you know about me \Nhaving the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.89,0:01:23.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Simple reasoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.83,0:01:27.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Judging by the injuries to Archer, I could tell what had happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.21,0:01:32.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the center of it was Scar, \Nthe scarred man.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.30,0:01:35.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then I heard that \Nyou two had fled.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.29,0:01:40.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,King Bradley only wants one thing: the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.53,0:01:42.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You knew?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.12,0:01:44.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,About the Führer \Nbeing a homunculus?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.60,0:01:50.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey now, how many years do you think I spent in the 5th Laboratory, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.27,0:01:54.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They used to go there, \Nalong with that other one.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.05,0:01:55.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That other one?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.40,0:01:58.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one who raised and \Nis leading the homunculi.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.88,0:02:01.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a moment. \NBy any chance, is that person...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.37,0:02:02.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll talk later.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.95,0:02:06.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have obtained something that \Nthey wanted so bad they can't stand it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.55,0:02:12.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, bring it out! \NA real, genuine Philosopher's Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.29,0:02:16.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please do not touch me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.90,0:02:23.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I{\i0} am the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.11,0:02:27.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a surprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.05,0:02:30.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's the reason why \NEdward-kun didn't come, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.21,0:02:33.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. We don't know \Nwhat will happen to my body
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.21,0:02:35.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if we use the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.85,0:02:38.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,at least not until \Nwe carefully research it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.07,0:02:41.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said he wanted to do something about the homunculi before then.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.32,0:02:44.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know that Brother \Nis worried about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.32,0:02:47.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I want to return Brother to the way he used to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.49,0:02:49.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you know of \Na way to do that...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.20,0:02:53.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course I do. I will teach you \Nhow to use the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.07,0:02:58.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I want you to \Nlet me use its power as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.28,0:03:00.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.74,0:03:08.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.78,0:03:14.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who obtain it are set free from the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.35,0:03:18.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need to pay a price \Nin order to obtain something, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.30,0:03:22.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We sought it and found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.04,0:05:11.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Most of it has been disposed of.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.33,0:05:13.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These books are all worthless.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.43,0:05:16.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What kind of person was Dante-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.55,0:05:20.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was a great alchemist, \None who inherited this crest.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.65,0:05:22.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or that's what I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.05,0:05:23.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What you thought?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.83,0:05:27.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was positively ingenious in her knowledge of alchemy
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.92,0:05:29.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and hid it completely.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.72,0:05:32.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Doesn't that go without saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.13,0:05:36.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, we encrypt our secrets \Nabout alchemy and record them too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.41,0:05:38.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was incorrigible about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.88,0:05:42.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If alchemy was for the good of mankind, why hide it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.03,0:05:47.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She chose to live a life in the forest, where she wouldn't meet anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.41,0:05:49.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For what reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.54,0:05:57.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought you would be thrilled.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.09,0:06:02.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does this mean that you were just another ordinary person?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.55,0:06:04.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm leaving the forest \Nto live in the city—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.81,0:06:08.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,among the people who need me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.81,0:06:11.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So you're going to live your life \Nfor the gratitude of others?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.44,0:06:17.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then why don't you just go ahead and enlist as a State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.37,0:06:19.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.83,0:06:21.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.51,0:06:22.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.58,0:06:25.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you like other people?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.02,0:06:28.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could I like them?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.56,0:06:32.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're selfish creatures without any merit.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.94,0:06:37.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They learn how to use a little gunpowder, and there is nothing but war.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.52,0:06:41.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they were to learn all of the secrets of alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.21,0:06:42.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,how much calamity do you think would come about?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.96,0:06:46.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, I am human! \NAnd so are you!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.92,0:06:57.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was one name that you could never utter in her presence:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.55,0:07:02.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hohenheim of Light.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.29,0:07:05.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,M-My old man?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.13,0:07:09.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Looks like she couldn't \Nbring herself to throw this away.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.36,0:07:17.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a love letter from \NHohenheim to Dante.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.83,0:07:22.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,J-Just a minute! I met Dante-san, and she was pretty old.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.88,0:07:25.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She looked like she was twenty years older than my old man.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.82,0:07:28.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not what the issue is.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.16,0:07:30.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This has the year written on it \Nin the Christian calendar.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.86,0:07:32.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Christian calendar?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.32,0:07:36.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was based on an ancient religion that isn't practiced now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.80,0:07:38.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to this, the letter...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.38,0:07:41.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was written four hundred years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.90,0:07:48.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What does it mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.48,0:07:50.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.24,0:07:52.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe the names are just the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.85,0:07:56.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's possible that the one \Ncontrolling all the homunculi is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.22,0:07:58.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're jumping to conclusions.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.18,0:08:02.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But are you prepared for that, \Njust in case?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.59,0:08:11.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry I couldn't be of any help.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.43,0:08:15.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's okay. This is something we'll do by ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.40,0:08:17.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.95,0:08:23.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.66,0:08:27.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You fool...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.83,0:08:31.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.64,0:08:46.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's about to happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.24,0:08:49.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If war breaks out in the north,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.26,0:08:51.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it'll be different from the civil uprisings \Nwe've had up to now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.35,0:08:53.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry I'm laid up \Nat a time like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.18,0:08:56.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's just about time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.95,0:09:00.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Havoc, you won't get lonely.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.30,0:09:01.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll have another friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.39,0:09:04.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant Fuery, \Nsome nasty athlete's foot
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.96,0:09:07.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was discovered during your examination the other day.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.45,0:09:09.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It has already spread to your brain.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.43,0:09:12.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's how it goes. \NYou won't be moving out either.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.78,0:09:23.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.01,0:09:26.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Surely, you jest.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.54,0:09:34.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Clearly, the north is \Nengaging in military actions,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.10,0:09:37.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and we cannot help but say that it would be foolish
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.80,0:09:42.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to overlook this and take up the matter \Nof our already established borders again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.22,0:09:45.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, the Führer has \Ncome to a wise conclusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.73,0:09:49.56,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,We will gather our forces in the Briggs Mountains, \Nalong the border to the north,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.90,0:09:53.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,where we will purge \Nany and all infiltrators!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.29,0:09:56.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You who are assembled here today \Nare the best of the best
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.57,0:09:59.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and will be the first ones there!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.68,0:10:03.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry for all of these \Ndifficult missions in a row.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.58,0:10:05.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I feel it's an honor.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.81,0:10:10.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I believe the suspicions \Nabout you are unfounded.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.19,0:10:11.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is my proof of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.92,0:10:15.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will live up to your expectations, \NYour Excellency.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.82,0:10:18.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wish you good luck, \NBrigadier General Roy Mustang.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.11,0:10:24.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col. Alex Louis Armstrong, support him well for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.35,0:10:28.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir. However, with our main forces \Nconcentrated in the north,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.18,0:10:30.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am concerned for \Nthe defense of Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.82,0:10:34.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not worry. \NFrank Archer is eager to help.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.38,0:10:35.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Archer?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.60,0:10:38.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean, that man is still alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.07,0:11:18.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A job well done, Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.52,0:11:22.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are no legends of the \NPhilosopher's Stone in the north.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.61,0:11:23.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even by fanning the flames of war,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.81,0:11:27.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there isn't anyone there who will be \Ndriven to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.29,0:11:31.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's all right. Your purpose this time \Nis the leadership of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.42,0:11:35.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyone who comes near the \NPhilosopher's Stone is destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.45,0:11:38.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who are soldiers \Nare not excepted.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.47,0:11:40.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then it's not just Mustang.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.67,0:11:46.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No. Everyone who was involved with \Nthe Hughes affair is going to die in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.02,0:11:47.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Courtesy of Envy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.23,0:11:49.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you mean me, I'm right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.85,0:11:55.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, I thought I told you \Nto wait up north.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.53,0:11:57.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that {\i1}he{\i0} was here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.17,0:11:58.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're being rude, Envy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.08,0:12:00.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Out of my way, you human poser!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.70,0:12:03.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't have you \Ntalk to him like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.19,0:12:09.06,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,He is a homunculus that appears to age \Nlike a person and is one of my masterpieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.06,0:12:10.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is he?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.46,0:12:12.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"He" who?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.50,0:12:19.43,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,That guy! The same way you made Pride and\N Greed! He's toying with me—toying with us!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.38,0:12:22.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hohenheim of Light?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.42,0:12:25.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's here, right?! Where is he?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.55,0:12:27.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You miss your birth father?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.02,0:12:32.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is he?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.62,0:12:33.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.74,0:12:34.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're lying!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.97,0:12:37.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way he could die!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.20,0:12:39.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm the one who will \Nkill him, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.73,0:12:43.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I disrupted the union of \Nhis spirit, body, and mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.45,0:12:44.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's as good as dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.89,0:12:49.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not true! It's not true! Why didn't you tell me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.20,0:12:51.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was supposed to be mine! \NMine! Mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.40,0:12:53.32,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.85,0:12:54.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His sons are still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.73,0:12:56.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To hell with them!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.23,0:13:00.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even once you hear that they have obtained a Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.62,0:13:04.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They have a Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.30,0:13:09.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. At this rate, those boys are going to take everything back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.21,0:13:11.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't let them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.48,0:13:13.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's unfair, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.55,0:13:16.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those boys getting to take everything back,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.31,0:13:20.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,while you, who should be \Nhis dearest son...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.52,0:13:21.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,are unable to obtain anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.73,0:13:23.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to see them...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.90,0:13:27.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the expressions on their faces when the \NPhilosopher's Stone is taken from them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.74,0:13:32.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their expressions when they lose everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.96,0:13:39.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"I'm going to Tucker-san's place."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.44,0:13:43.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shou Tucker. I thought he ran away at Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.71,0:13:47.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on. Why do you think Tucker called him there?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.15,0:13:52.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's obvious. To complete that useless Chimera of his.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.18,0:13:54.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's his daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.76,0:13:58.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tucker learned a lot of things from the 5th Laboratory,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.02,0:13:59.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,including things about \Nthe Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.82,0:14:01.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And since he knows,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.37,0:14:05.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Fullmetal brothers will know \Nhow to use the Philosopher's Stone too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.96,0:14:08.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you thinking, Lust?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.86,0:14:12.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrath,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.80,0:14:14.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,take care of everything \Nelse here for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.70,0:14:17.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're leaving?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.18,0:14:18.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a good boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.65,0:14:28.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My word, your brother is a genius.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.66,0:14:33.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He struck upon this seven-sided transmutation circle right on the spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.50,0:14:35.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean, you just copied it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.84,0:14:38.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd like you to say that \NI expanded on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.51,0:14:42.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But still, the fact is, Edward-kun came very close to the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.42,0:14:49.41,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,He probably realized that this method could be used to activate the Philosopher's Stone as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.03,0:14:54.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother was concerned \Nabout my body.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.78,0:14:59.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He just thought you should be giving precedence to regenerating your body.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.96,0:15:04.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He doesn't seem to have any interest in using the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.26,0:15:06.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.09,0:15:08.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's probably because...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.43,0:15:13.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.03,0:15:15.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could you come \Nover here for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.94,0:15:31.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tucker-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.50,0:15:33.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to have you \Npay me in advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.96,0:15:37.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry. \NBringing Nina back to life
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.07,0:15:41.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,will be nothing at all for a \NPhilosopher's Stone as huge as this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.04,0:15:43.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please wait! I'm still...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.77,0:15:47.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina, Nina, it will be soon now...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.00,0:15:48.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tucker-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.39,0:15:52.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.84,0:15:54.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.53,0:16:00.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dumbass!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.97,0:16:04.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're looking well, for someone being pursued by the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.15,0:16:07.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard about what you are \Nfrom my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.95,0:16:09.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am who I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.36,0:16:10.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.64,0:16:13.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't try anything funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.34,0:16:15.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you hiding?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.53,0:16:19.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you I knew \Nwhat you were!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.21,0:16:23.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrath!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.71,0:16:26.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Today's the day \Nwhen I will have them!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.94,0:16:29.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, but they're not for sale!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.54,0:16:32.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,S-Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.47,0:16:40.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrath!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.77,0:16:42.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're going to beg for your life, \NI'm not listening.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.75,0:16:46.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, that's all right. If you want my arm or leg, take them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.49,0:16:49.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've got the greatest \NAutomail mechanic around.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.59,0:16:52.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She'll give me something even cooler.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.62,0:16:53.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.61,0:16:56.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But answer me one thing—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.45,0:16:59.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if you take my arm and leg from me \Nand attach them to yourself,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.29,0:17:01.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,will that make you human?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.87,0:17:04.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if I have to use Automail—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.82,0:17:08.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,even if my whole body becomes armor, \Nso what? I'm still human.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.38,0:17:10.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.29,0:17:11.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.70,0:17:16.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust! What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.64,0:17:22.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get him! If you don't kill him, \NI'm telling you-know-who on you!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.14,0:17:34.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get him, Lust!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.91,0:17:37.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want to become human too, \Ndon't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.25,0:17:40.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If there is a Philosopher's Stone, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.06,0:17:46.03,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Your little brother went off to Tucker's place \Nand is learning how to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.46,0:17:51.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you find out how...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.33,0:17:54.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust, what are you saying?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.58,0:17:55.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.76,0:17:58.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,make me human?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.10,0:18:00.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.45,0:18:03.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think you're doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.80,0:18:04.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.83,0:18:10.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cut it out. Do you seriously think I would make you guys human?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.19,0:18:11.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.15,0:18:17.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you were to make us human, \Nyou wouldn't be chased after any longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.15,0:18:18.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your enemies would be gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.97,0:18:22.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You traitor!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.88,0:18:30.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What were we told?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.22,0:18:34.34,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,You heard! Once we delivered the \NPhilosopher's Stone, we would be made human!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.34,0:18:36.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't believe it...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.57,0:18:42.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You-know-who only wants the Philosopher's Stone to go on living.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.48,0:18:45.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why there have \Nbeen so many wars.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.27,0:18:50.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That person is not going to make us human.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.65,0:18:53.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's okay. I...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.41,0:18:57.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,will become human \Nunder my own power!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.79,0:19:02.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's just as I was told. \N"You can't trust Lust."
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.95,0:19:04.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're a nuisance, lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.70,0:19:19.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.08,0:19:29.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have to hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.66,0:19:31.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sloth is going after your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.68,0:19:33.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know where Tucker is?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.77,0:19:35.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The factory where he worked
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.78,0:19:38.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,before he became \Na State Alchemist is close.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.15,0:19:43.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait. Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.42,0:19:45.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though \NI promised you anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.80,0:19:47.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.90,0:19:51.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I{\i0} should be the one asking why! \NWhy do you want to become human?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.38,0:19:55.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys are immortal and can \Nremain in your present forms forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.35,0:19:58.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure why, but you \Nlook like you enjoy your lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.28,0:20:01.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So why would you want to become human again?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.92,0:20:06.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's such a cruel thing \Nfor you to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.63,0:20:10.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, why do you have to return your brother back to the way he was?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.40,0:20:15.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.85,0:20:18.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.11,0:20:22.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This "you-know-who" person who's in charge of you—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.15,0:20:25.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,by any chance, \Nis it someone I know?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.87,0:20:28.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good question.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.83,0:20:31.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once I become human, \NI wouldn't mind telling you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.88,0:20:34.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't forget,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.48,0:20:38.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm still carrying your weakness!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.27,0:20:40.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.32,0:20:43.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way I could forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.56,0:20:50.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina, is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.47,0:20:55.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.20,0:20:55.73,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,That's great, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.17,0:21:02.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alphonse-kun. Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.32,0:21:04.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Nina.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.28,0:21:10.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See? She knows what I'm saying.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.65,0:21:12.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right, Nina?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.58,0:21:15.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Call me Papa, Nina.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.01,0:21:17.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Her soul...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.70,0:21:28.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Congratulations, Shou Tucker.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.01,0:21:31.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a magnificent human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.82,0:21:33.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.43,0:21:37.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not interested in \Nyour soulless doll.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.57,0:21:41.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Only a powerful will is able to \Nkeep a soul set in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.32,0:21:44.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like that wasn't \Npossible for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.78,0:21:48.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come along, Alphonse Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.61,0:21:53.79,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,We can't very well let such a precious Philosopher's Stone be diminished any further.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.79,0:21:54.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Diminished?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.39,0:22:05.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, Brother, is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.94,0:22:09.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\t(1630,3550,\c&H000000&,\3c&H000000&,\4c&H000000&)}the Philosopher's Stone?!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.72,0:23:40.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.39,0:23:43.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 47: "Sealing the Homunculus"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.88,0:23:45.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look, Sloth.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.15,0:23:48.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your weakness is right here.
